            <ArticleTitle>Differential effects of sodium meglumine calcium metrizoate on the inotropic state of normal and ischemic myocardium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>499-501</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sodium meglumine calcium metrizoate was injected into isolated blood-perfused canine hearts to evaluate the effect of contrast agents containing calcium on normal and ischemic myocardium. Under normal perfusion pressure and mild ischemia, this contrast agent produced a positive inotropic effect, but during profound ischemia, this positive effect was followed by a period of myocardial depression. These findings indicate that the addition of an inotropic agent to contrast medium can produce a paradoxical depressant effect which can be deleterious to the ischemic myocardium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
